Adjusted when the coronary spell is learned and becomes maxable.
There's long been no reason for a shaman to invest practices in the
skunk discipline past 80%, as the coronary spell was learned at 75%
and became maxable at 80%.

Because coronary is very powerful, is the capstone ability in an
advanced discipline, and to make the final 20% in the skunk discipline
meaningful, coronary has been updated to first unlock at 81%, becoming
fully maxable at 100%. This will have the side effect of increasing its
damage by around 8%.

Shamans who had previously stopped their skunk learning at 80% will find
they can no longer use coronary at all, though any previous hones will
be retained as the spell's potential is increased by investing further
practices in the skunk discipline.

Characters without available practices can consider respeccing at their
guildmaster to reallocate their existing learnedness.

Note: A total of 20 practices is required to take an advanced discipline
from 80% to 100%. This is standard across all advanced disciplines.
